# Goliath Daydreamer: "Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell from your hand, exile that card with a dream counter on it
# instead of putting it into your graveyard as it resolves." Bot1 casts Goliath on turn 1 and on turn 3 a Lightning Bolt from
# the hand: the Bolt does its damage, then is exiled with a dream counter (the graveyard stays empty). "Whenever this creature
# attacks, you may cast a spell from among cards you own in exile with dream counters on them without paying its mana cost":
# the attack casts that Bolt again for nothing; cast from exile it is not cast from the hand, so it goes to the graveyard.

